              "text": "zhōumò is built from zhōu 'week' and mò 'end'. The second is inherited from Middle Chinese mat (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'the tip of a tree' and 'end'. The first character is recorded there as tsyuw, 'a full circuit'; the sense week is not given, so how it came to name the week is not settled."
            }
